    <h2>What is ID Verification?</h2>
    <p>OkayDoc is EMAS eKYC's document authentication component that verifies whether identity documents are genuine, legitimate, and unaltered. Using patented AI algorithms and image analysis, OkayDoc examines ID cards, passports, and driver's licenses for approximately 20 different security features — including holograms, ghost images, microprints, watermarks, and UV elements — to determine authenticity in seconds.</p>
    <p>Unlike manual inspection that relies on human judgment and reference guides, OkayDoc uses machine learning models trained on millions of documents to detect even sophisticated forgeries. It includes anti-spoofing capabilities to identify photographed documents, screen displays, and color-printed copies, as well as anti-tampering detection to flag altered or modified documents. OkayDoc enables businesses to prevent identity fraud, comply with KYC regulations, and protect themselves from financial losses.</p>

    <h2>What Problems Does It Solve?</h2>
    <h3>Fraudulent Documents Are Increasingly Sophisticated</h3>
    <p>Modern identity fraud has evolved beyond simple photocopies. Criminal organizations now produce fake IDs with sophisticated printing techniques, replica holograms, and security features that look genuine to the untrained eye. In 2024, financial institutions lost over $5.8 billion globally to identity fraud, with fraudulent documents being a primary attack vector. Traditional manual verification cannot keep pace with these forgery techniques.</p>

    <h3>Manual Document Inspection Doesn't Scale</h3>
    <p>Banks, fintech companies, and other regulated businesses traditionally employed specialized staff to manually inspect ID documents during customer onboarding. This approach has critical limitations: it's slow, expensive, only available during business hours, and requires extensive training. Human inspectors cannot consistently detect sophisticated forgeries, especially when processing hundreds of documents daily.</p>

    <h3>Digital Onboarding Creates New Vulnerability</h3>
    <p>The shift to digital customer onboarding has created new opportunities for fraudsters. Without physical document inspection, criminals can submit photographed fake IDs, screen-captured images, or color-printed copies. These "presentation attacks" are increasingly common, with some platforms reporting that 15-20% of submitted documents are spoofed or tampered with.</p>

    <h3>Regulatory Compliance Requirements Are Mandatory</h3>
    <p>Financial services, telecommunications, and other regulated industries must comply with KYC and AML regulations that require verifying customer identity documents. Regulatory authorities across ASEAN are increasing enforcement, with significant fines for businesses that fail to properly authenticate customer IDs. Manual verification processes struggle to maintain consistent standards and documentation.</p>

    <h2>How Businesses Use It</h2>
    <h3>Digital Banks and Financial Services</h3>
    <p>Digital-only banks and fintech platforms integrate OkayDoc into their account opening workflows to verify customer identity documents in real-time. When a prospective customer uploads their passport or national ID card during the application process, OkayDoc automatically analyzes the document for authenticity, checking security features and detecting common fraud attempts. Within seconds, the system provides a verification result, allowing instant account approval for legitimate customers.</p>

    <h3>Cryptocurrency and Digital Asset Exchanges</h3>
    <p>Crypto trading platforms use OkayDoc to meet increasingly strict KYC regulations while processing high volumes of identity verifications. The system detects fraudulent documents used to create accounts for money laundering, sanctions evasion, and other financial crimes.</p>

    <h3>Telecommunications and SIM Registration</h3>
    <p>Mobile network operators across ASEAN use OkayDoc to comply with government-mandated SIM card registration that requires verifying subscriber identity documents. OkayDoc authenticates IDs at retail locations and through online channels, preventing the use of fake documents for anonymous SIM cards.</p>

